From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] st: keep the scissor for a scissored clear drawn as a quad

A scissored glClear on a driver without scissored clears is drawn as a
quad covering the scissor rectangle, with the scissor disabled. Tiling
drivers size a render pass by the scissor, so the clear counted as
drawing the whole framebuffer and the pass loaded and stored every
tile. A compositor clears the stencil this way for every clip region
of more than one rectangle; on a Raspberry Pi 5 (v3d) at 3840x2160 a
partial redraw of two small areas paid for a full-screen pass.

The scissor state is current (st_validate_state() ran) and matches the
quad, so leave it enabled while drawing the quad. What is drawn is
unchanged.
---
 src/mesa/state_tracker/st_cb_clear.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_cb_clear.c b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_cb_clear.c
--- a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_cb_clear.c
+++ b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_cb_clear.c
@@ -279,6 +279,14 @@ clear_with_quad(struct gl_context *ctx, unsigned clear_buffers)
    cso_set_sample_coverage(cso, 1.0f, false);
    cso_set_min_samples(cso, 1);
    st->clear.raster.multisample = st->state.fb_num_samples > 1;
+   /* The quad covers only the scissor rectangle. Keep the scissor (which
+    * st_validate_state() left current) enabled as well: a tiling driver
+    * sizes the render pass by the scissor, and a quad drawn with it off
+    * counts as drawing the whole framebuffer, so a scissored clear (a
+    * compositor clearing the stencil for a clip region) made the pass load
+    * and store every tile.
+    */
+   st->clear.raster.scissor = (ctx->Scissor.EnableFlags & 1) != 0;
    cso_set_rasterizer(cso, &st->clear.raster);
 
    /* viewport state: viewport matching window dims */
-- 
